  "summary_en": "ISO news release (8 March 2016) announcing ISO/TS 15066, a technical specification on safety of collaborative robots working alongside humans in industry. It complements ISO 10218 and gives guidance on speed and separation monitoring, power and force limiting, and pain-tolerance data to assess and control risks.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "ISO/TS 15066 gives safety guidance for collaborative robot workspaces, complementing ISO 10218-1/-2.",
   "Covers four collaborative techniques: safety-rated monitored stop, hand guiding, speed and separation monitoring, power and force limiting.",
   "Includes study data on pain tolerance thresholds of human body parts.",
   "Requires minimising sharp edges and protruding corners to limit impact severity.",
   "Expected to reassure designers and users and encourage investment in robotics."
